> I understood that, but the map of the city should be consistent with the map
> of the country. How big is the city (inhabitants, and kilometers)?

About 5x5km set on a grid with some houses set out a good 5-10 minutes
walking distance from the grid.
Population? About 5-10k. Enough to support a metropolitan-esque town,
but nothing huge.

I forsee cars being something rarely used, so roads should look more
like they're built for bicycles, and there should be a train/rail
system that runs from this town to Bertcad and other areas in short
amounts of time. Perhaps in Bertcad they're used a bit more, but I
don't forsee them being a necessity as Bertcad probably has a very
efficient public transportation system.

Harl!

So... Yeah.

